 - **AUTO-005 — Update reminders.** Project leads and initiative owners are reminded on the chosen cadence (weekly on a weekday, every two weeks) to post an update, with a prefilled draft (PROJ-010); missing updates are flagged on the project and in the initiative roll-up. *Acceptance:* a scheduled-run test that reminds one lead once per cadence and flags a missed update. *Status:* missing.
 - **AUTO-006 — Due-soon rules.** Rules on due dates can act before the due day (for example two days before: notify the assignee and move to the active cycle), complementing the fixed due-today and overdue reminders of NOTIFY-005. Inherited from ROLE-001: only Owners and Admins build or change workspace automation rules (role matrix). *Acceptance:* an AUTO-002 rule with a due-in-two-days trigger acting once per issue and date. *Status:* partial — `src/core/features/due-reminders/service.ts` (due-today and overdue notifications only).
 
+#### AUTO-007 — Private occurrence history after access changes
+
+*Tier:* Core · *From:* new
+
+**Requirement.** Recurring series history, recurrence results and Settings respect current access to previous occurrences, including after an occurrence moves to a private team, without revealing private issue status or widening authority.
+
+**Acceptance.**
+1. An operator who may manage a series but cannot currently read its previous occurrence learns no private issue status through series history, recurrence results or Settings. Moving the occurrence into a private team immediately applies current access; direct issue reads retain the same non-disclosing 404.
+2. A hidden previous occurrence being open versus completed produces no distinguishable series, history or scheduling outcome exposed to that operator. Skipped-versus-created results cannot disclose its status. Refusal or a uniform unavailable state preserves the hidden issue and reveals no private fields.
+3. Currently authorized owners and team members retain correct visible occurrence links, permitted history and normal weekly skip-while-open behavior. Safe handling after access loss neither widens anyone's authority nor alters the hidden issue.
+4. Native series history and ordinary Settings history at 1440 and 390 reflect the same safe result after an owner moves the issue and after its status changes. Worker restart and replay expose no retained private status and produce no duplicate occurrence effects.
+
