+# Vector contract rulings
+
+### RL-101 — AUTO-001 deferred at its lifetime FIX cap; separate privacy capability
+
+Date: 2026-11-06. Ruler: CT. Clauses: AUTO-001, AUTO-007.
+
+AUTO-001 is DEFER after two lifetime FIX verdicts. Neither original source/gate identity `352cadb54aad54198b16ba0c245079555d7d923a` nor corrected source/gate identity `133901fe0c6b727a95df326dfbf2d3b58869ca45` lands as gated. The original gate found missing Settings controls (A) and private previous-occurrence status disclosure (B). The required independent Opus review returned FIX1 on `133901fe0c6b727a95df326dfbf2d3b58869ca45`: A was resolved; the same B reproduced through scheduled and native doors and Settings at 1440 and 390. A Member received issue GET 404, while series history said skipped when the moved private issue was open and created after its completion. This is introduced privacy exposure absent on main, not a third new blocker.
+
+The lifetime two-FIX cap closes this AUTO-001 attempt. Its original scope, Status, full Gap and Evidence, frozen checks and two-FIX history remain intact; this ruling does not reopen or promote it. SD takes another buildable clause. AUTO-007 records one new Core privacy capability for the next planned Vector round, with missing Status and empty Evidence. It is not a third AUTO-001 repair. Its frozen future-build requirements are recorded in `docs/contract/AUTO-007-rubric.md`; they are requirements, never passing evidence.
+
+Original deployment-inventory notes, the 0126 migration collision and CI failures remain provenance only. This contract pass repairs no tooling and transfers no proof. Existing source, stack, review, provider and release holds remain. The supported CT review hold remains pending independent Opus review on the exact candidate head; this ruling authorizes no release, submission or landing.
